## Permitted Use

You may use and modify the software only for:

1. your own internal business purposes;
2. non-commercial research, education, evaluation, or experimentation;
3. personal use;
4. internal development, testing, governance, automation, compliance, AI-agent management, software-development workflows, or operational workflows within your own organization.

You may distribute the software or provide it to others only if you do so free of charge and for non-commercial purposes.

For clarity, internal business use by an organization is permitted under this license, even if that organization is commercial, provided the software is not itself sold, hosted, embedded, bundled, white-labeled, sublicensed, commercially distributed, or commercially provided to third parties.

## Commercial Use Restrictions

You may not, without a separate written commercial license from the licensor:

1. sell, rent, lease, sublicense, or otherwise commercially provide the software to any third party;

2. offer the software, modified software, or any material part of the software as a hosted service, managed service, SaaS product, platform service, API service, embedded service, or similar offering;

3. provide third parties with direct or indirect access to the software, including through a user interface, API, agent runtime, governance runtime, automation service, compliance service, developer tool, hosted control plane, or managed deployment;

4. use the software to operate, govern, monitor, automate, control, or manage third-party systems, repositories, agents, workflows, data, users, compliance processes, or operations as part of a paid product, paid platform, paid consulting deliverable, managed service, or other commercial offering;

5. embed, bundle, package, integrate, or distribute the software as part of a commercial product or service provided to third parties;

6. white-label, rebrand, resell, or market the software, modified software, or substantially equivalent software functionality as your own product or service;

7. commercially distribute modified versions of the software;

8. use the software in a manner that provides substantially the same functional value as the licensor’s hosted offerings, enterprise licenses, commercial licenses, commercial support offerings, or managed services to third parties.

For clarity, you may use the software internally within your own organization, including for internal governance, compliance, automation, AI-agent management, software-development workflows, research, evaluation, and internal operational tooling.

For clarity, a consultant, contractor, systems integrator, managed service provider, or similar service provider may use the software for its own internal business operations under this license. However, using the software to operate, govern, monitor, automate, control, or manage client or third-party systems, agents, workflows, repositories, compliance processes, data, users, or operations as part of a paid service requires a separate written commercial license.

## Generated Code and Generated Outputs

Generated code, generated documentation, generated schemas, generated manifests, generated policies, generated tests, generated configuration, generated artifacts, and other generated materials that are included in this repository or distributed as part of SEA-Forge are part of the software and are licensed under the same license terms that apply to the files, directories, or components in which they appear.

For clarity, generated materials committed to the SEA-Forge repository are covered by the SEA-Forge Sustainable Use License unless they are:

1. enterprise-only components covered by `LICENSE_EE.md`;
2. third-party components covered by their original licenses; or
3. separately licensed components expressly identified in this repository.

Generated outputs created by users outside this repository are not automatically subject to the SEA-Forge Sustainable Use License merely because they were generated by SEA-Forge.

Users may own, use, modify, distribute, commercialize, and license their user generated outputs under terms of their choosing, provided those outputs do not include copied, modified, embedded, bundled, or derivative portions of SEA-Forge source code, SEA-Forge repository generated materials, enterprise-only components, or other separately licensed SEA-Forge materials except as separately permitted by this license or by a written commercial license.

For clarity:

- Repository generated materials are part of SEA-Forge and remain under the applicable SEA-Forge license.
- User generated outputs outside the SEA-Forge repository belong to the user and may be licensed separately.
- Using SEA-Forge to generate software, documentation, policies, schemas, manifests, specifications, reports, tests, workflows, applications, architecture artifacts, cognitive artifacts, knowledge graphs, information products, or other artifacts does not by itself place those generated outputs under the SEA-Forge license.
- You may use SEA-Forge internally to generate proprietary software for your own organization.
- You may use SEA-Forge internally to generate documentation, policies, specifications, architecture artifacts, cognitive artifacts, knowledge graphs, information products, or operational workflows for your own organization.
- You may commercialize user generated outputs, provided SEA-Forge itself is not copied, modified, embedded, bundled, hosted, sublicensed, distributed, white-labeled, or provided as part of that commercial offering without a separate written commercial license.
- Embedding, copying, redistributing, hosting, sublicensing, commercially distributing, or white-labeling SEA-Forge itself, including generated repository code that is part of SEA-Forge, remains subject to this license.

